# Code owners for dair-containment-loop.
#
# Owners must be a GitHub username or an @org/team. A bare organization name
# (@irocsecurity) is NOT valid and fails silently.
#
# The owner must have WRITE access to this repository. If you later add other
# maintainers, create @irocsecurity/maintainers, give that team write access,
# and replace the entries below with it.
#
# Enforced only when "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled in the
# main-protection ruleset. That setting is what makes an outside contributor's
# pull request require approval from the organization before it can merge.

*                            @irocsecurity-own

# Paths where a mistake is most expensive. Listed explicitly so a change here
# is visibly a code-owner change even if the catch-all above is ever relaxed.
/.github/workflows/          @irocsecurity-own
/.github/CODEOWNERS          @irocsecurity-own
/dair_containment/loop.py    @irocsecurity-own
/dair_containment/auth.py    @irocsecurity-own
/LICENSE                     @irocsecurity-own
/NOTICE                      @irocsecurity-own
/TRADEMARK.md                @irocsecurity-own
/SECURITY.md                 @irocsecurity-own
